00:30:35.333 --> 00:30:38.167
- He'd drop off, then we'd dial him in.
- So? Can you do that?

487
00:30:38.250 --> 00:30:41.375
We risk losing contact. He's on the move.
Plus the time it takes.

488
00:30:41.458 --> 00:30:44.667
STRATCOM is asking for
our launch instructions for retaliation.

489
00:30:45.167 --> 00:30:46.875
- Like, right now.
- Okay. All right.

490
00:30:48.917 --> 00:30:51.333
Sir, we're having technical issues
with the president.

491
00:30:51.417 --> 00:30:54.125
I'm gonna get you someone
who can speak for him right now.

492
00:30:54.208 --> 00:30:55.208
Please hold.

493
00:30:55.583 --> 00:30:58.667
Billy, I want you to go and get my cell.
Get yours too.

494
00:30:59.167 --> 00:31:00.375
- Ma'am.
- Just go.

495
00:31:00.458 --> 00:31:01.458
Why are we launching?

496
00:31:01.500 --> 00:31:03.708
Quickly. I'm asking you.
I can handle this.

497
00:31:05.500 --> 00:31:07.417
Not sure. You'll have to try DOD.

498
00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:10.000
Who's in charge there? Can you put him on?

499
00:31:10.083 --> 00:31:12.667
Gail, can you monitor the NSCC?

500
00:32:17.542 --> 00:32:20.208
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Hey, Mom. Um…

501
00:32:20.708 --> 00:32:22.458
Yeah, no, everything's, uh…

502
00:32:26.292 --> 00:32:28.875
Yeah, no, no, I'm good.
I promise you I am…

503
00:32:29.375 --> 00:32:30.458
I'm doing great.

504
00:32:32.042 --> 00:32:33.625
Okay.

505
00:32:35.917 --> 00:32:37.292
Yeah, no, I'm, uh…

506
00:32:37.792 --> 00:32:39.583
Yeah, I'm working hard. I'm

507
00:32:40.958 --> 00:32:42.208
doing my best.

508
00:32:47.125 --> 00:32:48.125
Yeah.

509
00:32:50.208 --> 00:32:52.958
No, I just… I just wanted to call you
and, you know,

510
00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:55.167
tell you I love you.

511
00:32:55.917 --> 00:32:56.917
<i>Aw.</i>

512
00:33:02.333 --> 00:33:04.000
All right. I'll… I'll call you later. Um…

513
00:33:04.083 --> 00:33:06.250
Yeah, I gotta go.
They're calling me right now.

514
00:33:22.708 --> 00:33:25.125
<i>They've got five minutes.
How far is anyone gonna get?</i>

515
00:33:25.208 --> 00:33:27.042
<i>They can at least shelter in place.</i>

516
00:33:27.125 --> 00:33:29.125
Do you think hiding under desks
is gonna help them?

517
00:33:29.167 --> 00:33:31.708
There's a car outside.
Driver says you're on some kind of list.

518
00:33:31.792 --> 00:33:33.458
- "Hasty Access."
- Who's downstairs?

519
00:33:33.542 --> 00:33:34.917
Some guy's here to take Cathy.

520
00:33:37.500 --> 00:33:39.500
- I'm a DE, Mike.
- What does that mean?

521
00:33:41.625 --> 00:33:43.250
Designated evacuee.

522
00:33:44.125 --> 00:33:46.208
It means
she gets to ride this out at Raven Rock.

523
00:33:46.292 --> 00:33:48.750
You chose me as your alternate.

524
00:33:49.667 --> 00:33:52.875
There's no threat to DC. There might not
even be a threat to Chicago.

525
00:33:52.958 --> 00:33:54.708
She's barely done her job for a month.

526
00:33:55.542 --> 00:33:57.250
Why does she get to be rescued?

527
00:34:00.875 --> 00:34:01.875
Come on.

528
00:34:03.917 --> 00:34:06.375
- He's checking in.
- I'll update you when we get there.

529
00:34:06.458 --> 00:34:08.083
Yeah. Come on. We're moving out.

530
00:34:12.583 --> 00:34:14.917
Hey, what's going on up there?
Where's everyone going?

531
00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:18.083
Try his secretary! Somebody!
Secretary, I don't give a…

532
00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:20.000
Go home.

533
00:34:40.000 --> 00:34:43.542
Beijing Station reports
the PSC is convening an emergency session.

534
00:34:44.167 --> 00:34:46.417
Yes. Yes,
I can get that for you right away.

535
00:34:48.167 --> 00:34:51.208
- Situation Room. Walker.
- <i>Put me back on the NSCC.</i>

536
00:34:51.292 --> 00:34:52.958
- Is it Russia's?
- <i>He denied it.</i>

537
00:34:53.042 --> 00:34:55.958
<i>Said it might be Pyongyang. But he swears
they had nothing to do with it.</i>

538
00:34:56.042 --> 00:34:57.042
Why are they mobilizing?

539
00:34:57.083 --> 00:34:58.958
<i>They're seeing our B-2s go airborne.</i>

540
00:34:59.042 --> 00:35:01.125
<i>Now put me back on the fucking conference.</i>

541
00:35:10.250 --> 00:35:13.250
Look. Look, as I told you,
I am not fully briefed yet,

542
00:35:13.333 --> 00:35:15.625
but I promise
I am doing my best to chase it down.

543
00:35:15.708 --> 00:35:17.167
You don't know why he bailed?

544
00:35:17.250 --> 00:35:19.917
- Is the president in Washington?
- Look, I…

545
00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:21.333
A military hero…

546
00:35:21.417 --> 00:35:22.792
Where should we go?

547
00:35:22.875 --> 00:35:25.458
The American public deserves
to know what's happening.

548
00:35:25.542 --> 00:35:27.375
Excuse me.
Sorry. Do you know what's going on?

549
00:35:27.458 --> 00:35:28.625
You should leave if you can.

550
00:35:28.708 --> 00:35:29.792
Are the American...

551
00:35:29.875 --> 00:35:31.292
- Sorry.
- Where are you going?

552
00:35:31.375 --> 00:35:32.875
What is happening?

553
00:35:38.042 --> 00:35:43.000
Yes, we've got Governor on line two,
and we're merging the calls now.

554
00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:45.292
Thank you for your patience.

555
00:35:51.500 --> 00:35:54.125
Raven Rock is asking for
names and serial numbers

556
00:35:54.208 --> 00:35:55.792
of everyone still here on duty.

557
00:35:55.875 --> 00:35:57.875
Socials for civilians in case…

558
00:35:58.917 --> 00:36:02.583
If it's just Chicago, it's just Chicago,
but if we fire back…

559
00:36:02.667 --> 00:36:04.083
They need a dead list.

560
00:36:06.250 --> 00:36:07.417
Thanks.

561
00:36:30.375 --> 00:36:33.167
Yes. We have the governor on the line.

562
00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:38.000
Come on. Come on. Come on. Come on.

563
00:36:38.917 --> 00:36:39.917
Come on.

564
00:36:40.250 --> 00:36:42.458
All right, Liam. Watch your head, bud.
Watch your...

565
00:36:42.542 --> 00:36:44.542
I wanna do it by myself.

566
00:36:44.625 --> 00:36:46.625
Okay. Okay.

567
00:36:48.750 --> 00:36:49.875
- Hey.
- <i>Listen to me.</i>

568
00:36:49.958 --> 00:36:52.708
Get Liam, get in the car,
and just start driving.

569
00:36:52.792 --> 00:36:54.375
<i>Where? What are you talking about?</i>

570
00:36:54.458 --> 00:36:58.792
West. Go west. Go west as fast as you can.
Get away from any urban centers.

571
00:36:58.875 --> 00:37:00.958
- Liv, what the fuck? What's going on?
- <i>Listen.</i>

572
00:37:01.042 --> 00:37:05.375
<i>I'll call you. I love you. I love you.
Can you kiss Liam for me? Just kiss him.</i>

573
00:37:06.083 --> 00:37:07.125
Bye, bye, bye.

574
00:37:13.750 --> 00:37:14.750
Okay.

575
00:37:27.083 --> 00:37:29.042
- Miss Rogers?
- Yes. Yes.

576
00:38:12.750 --> 00:38:15.750
- <i>Sir, your nuclear forces are ready.</i>
- They'll wait, right?

577
00:38:16.917 --> 00:38:19.083
To see what happens before they retaliate.

578
00:38:20.125 --> 00:38:21.708
<i>What if he doesn't come back on?</i>

579
00:38:23.375 --> 00:38:24.792
<i>Decapitation event.</i>

580
00:38:24.875 --> 00:38:26.333
<i>We find the vice president…</i>

581
00:38:27.250 --> 00:38:31.292
- Any chance this lands in Lake Michigan?
- A lot of times, they don't even detonate.

582
00:38:31.375 --> 00:38:32.792
<i>All right, I'm here.</i>

583
00:38:33.375 --> 00:38:35.750
<i>- You'll need your SAS card, sir.
- Oh.</i>

584
00:38:37.333 --> 00:38:38.583
<i>It's in here somewhere.</i>

585
00:38:39.750 --> 00:38:40.750
<i>Right.</i>

586
00:38:41.167 --> 00:38:43.292
<i>Reminds me of when I was in college.</i>

587
00:38:46.375 --> 00:38:48.250
<i>You just, uh, read it aloud.</i>

588
00:38:49.083 --> 00:38:50.083
Hey.

589
00:38:51.125 --> 00:38:53.833
- <i>November, Delta, Oscar.</i>
- Come here.

590
00:38:54.417 --> 00:38:57.208
- <i>One, one, one, seven.</i>
- It's okay.

591
00:38:57.292 --> 00:38:59.750
<i>November, Delta, Oscar.</i>

592
00:38:59.833 --> 00:39:03.083
<i>One, one, one, seven.</i>

593
00:39:04.833 --> 00:39:07.208
<i>National command authority confirmed.</i>

594
00:39:08.833 --> 00:39:10.833
<i>Your orders, Mr. President?</i>

595
00:40:35.833 --> 00:40:37.167
{\an8}- Steve.
- General.

596
00:40:37.250 --> 00:40:41.083
{\an8}Goddamn! Lindor is a great shortstop, man.

597
00:40:41.167 --> 00:40:43.875
Tell me you watched
that All-Star game, please.

598
00:40:43.958 --> 00:40:45.667
Let your boys stay up that late?

599
00:40:46.583 --> 00:40:49.583
- Yours give you a choice?
- No. No, they do not.

600
00:40:55.875 --> 00:40:57.083
Call to arms!

601
00:40:57.708 --> 00:40:58.833
Fire!

602
00:41:04.083 --> 00:41:05.958
Ready!

603
00:41:06.042 --> 00:41:07.375
Fire at will!

604
00:41:24.833 --> 00:41:26.625
- This is awesome.
- Uh-huh.

605
00:41:26.708 --> 00:41:31.208
Well, 50,000 deaths in three days.
Awesome is one word.

606
00:41:55.625 --> 00:41:58.333
<i>This is the DDO
at the National Military Command Center</i>

607
00:41:58.417 --> 00:42:01.792
<i>with a top-secret SCI
national security conference</i>

608
00:42:01.875 --> 00:42:03.750
<i>for missile launch indications.</i>

609
00:42:03.833 --> 00:42:05.958
<i>All conferees, please stand by.</i>

610
00:42:17.542 --> 00:42:18.875
J3, are you tracking this?

611
00:42:18.958 --> 00:42:21.542
I don't remember anything
from the ops and intel briefing.

612
00:42:21.625 --> 00:42:24.000
It's news to me, Dan. I'll look into it.

613
00:42:37.667 --> 00:42:40.042
- Did you see that?
- On it.

614
00:42:41.333 --> 00:42:44.667
EDBC Whisper. Tracking
inbound ICBM in the Pacific theater.

615
00:42:45.500 --> 00:42:47.125
Attention on deck.

616
00:42:48.917 --> 00:42:50.875
Morning, everybody.
Please take your seats.

617
00:42:50.958 --> 00:42:53.667
- Morning, sir.
- What's the situation?

618
00:42:54.792 --> 00:42:57.125
Sir, missile-launch indications
in the Pacific theater.

619
00:42:57.208 --> 00:42:59.708
The DDO's standing up
a national security conference.

620
00:43:00.958 --> 00:43:03.625
Sir, no update yet,
but I'm hoping to have one soon.

621
00:43:08.167 --> 00:43:10.792
- Did you see that ball game last night?
- Yes, sir.

622
00:43:11.958 --> 00:43:13.500
You believe that Lindor?

623
00:43:14.042 --> 00:43:15.083
- I mean…
- Impressive.

624
00:43:15.167 --> 00:43:17.917
He is unbelievable.

625
00:43:21.583 --> 00:43:23.208
Yep, it's all good news.

626
00:43:28.458 --> 00:43:29.458
Okay.

627
00:43:30.875 --> 00:43:32.083
Okay, I'll tell him.

628
00:43:33.708 --> 00:43:34.708
Love you.

629
00:43:37.458 --> 00:43:40.167
My mom wants to know
if you're going to Helsinki next week.

630
00:43:40.250 --> 00:43:41.458
She must have…

631
00:43:42.208 --> 00:43:44.208
Must have seen it
on <i>The View </i>or something.

632
00:43:44.708 --> 00:43:46.292
No. No, I won't be there,

633
00:43:46.375 --> 00:43:48.833
but the briefing I wrote has
a really nice first-class seat,

634
00:43:48.917 --> 00:43:49.750
so that's great.

635
00:43:49.833 --> 00:43:52.333
If you're really not that happy,
I can talk to Marty.

636
00:43:52.417 --> 00:43:55.458
No, don't talk to Marty.
Staff director's a lateral move.

637
00:43:55.542 --> 00:43:59.083
- I can't go back to the Hill. It's a, uh…
- Hmm.

638
00:43:59.167 --> 00:44:01.292
- It's just…
- It's what?

639
00:44:02.875 --> 00:44:05.208
- It's a bad idea…
- Mmm.

640
00:44:05.750 --> 00:44:09.667
…to be working in such close proximity
to my radiant wife.

641
00:44:09.750 --> 00:44:13.500
You think that she'll inherit
your capacity for ass-kissing bullshit?

642
00:44:13.583 --> 00:44:15.917
Sorry.

643
00:44:16.750 --> 00:44:18.583
Hey, it… uh, it's Jake.

644
00:44:21.417 --> 00:44:22.417
Yeah.

645
00:44:26.750 --> 00:44:27.750
Bye.

646
00:44:33.667 --> 00:44:37.458
<i>The DSP satellite system
is generally reliable,</i>

647
00:44:37.542 --> 00:44:41.417
<i>but that will obviously be a focus
of our after-action.</i>

648
00:44:41.500 --> 00:44:43.667
{\an8}<i>So the launch could've been
land or sea-based?</i>

649
00:44:43.750 --> 00:44:46.292
<i>No, the DPRK don't have
an SSBN capability.</i>

650
00:44:46.375 --> 00:44:47.208
That we know of.

651
00:44:47.292 --> 00:44:49.750
<i>Beijing's been wanting
to test their Jin-class boats.</i>

652
00:44:49.833 --> 00:44:50.708
Eight sugars, please.

653
00:44:50.792 --> 00:44:52.917
<i>And we've been tracking
three Borei-class subs</i>

654
00:44:53.000 --> 00:44:55.125
<i>out of Vladivostok since last week.</i>

655
00:44:55.208 --> 00:44:57.208
<i>On top of their push into the Atlantic,</i>

656
00:44:57.292 --> 00:44:59.208
<i>I can't see 'em risking more sanctions.</i>

657
00:44:59.292 --> 00:45:01.875
<i>Uh, sir, on the, uh, North Korean front...</i>

658
00:45:01.958 --> 00:45:04.625
- Who is that?
<i>- Jake Baerington, sir.</i>

659
00:45:04.708 --> 00:45:06.042
<i>Dick Holland's deputy.</i>

660
00:45:06.125 --> 00:45:08.125
There's a reason
I didn't join the Navy, son.

661
00:45:08.208 --> 00:45:10.250
All that bouncing around's
making me seasick.

662
00:45:10.333 --> 00:45:13.042
<i>I'm sorry, sir. I just, um…
I'm almost at the White House.</i>

663
00:45:13.125 --> 00:45:14.458
<i>I just wanted to say,</i>

664
00:45:15.125 --> 00:45:18.333
<i>well, we do know that the KPA
have been chasing sub capabilities,</i>

665
00:45:18.417 --> 00:45:21.917
okay, and previous leaps
in booster design and TELs

666
00:45:22.000 --> 00:45:23.750
have gone undetected till roll out.

667
00:45:23.833 --> 00:45:25.667
<i>Mr. Baerington? All due respect...</i>

668
00:45:25.750 --> 00:45:26.958
- Thank you.
<i>- Hello?</i>

669
00:45:27.542 --> 00:45:28.625
<i>Mr. Baerington?</i>

670
00:45:29.917 --> 00:45:31.500
<i>Did we lose him?</i>

671
00:45:31.583 --> 00:45:32.792
Mr. Baerington?

672
00:45:32.875 --> 00:45:34.000
Hello? Sir?

673
00:45:37.042 --> 00:45:38.042
Fuck.

674
00:45:39.875 --> 00:45:40.875
Sir.

675
00:45:42.208 --> 00:45:44.583
I do think we need to upgrade
our salvage operations.

676
00:45:44.667 --> 00:45:47.583
We're leaving potentially valuable
intelligence on the ocean floor...

677
00:45:47.667 --> 00:45:48.667
Sir.

678
00:45:49.167 --> 00:45:51.375
Uh, excuse me a moment. What?

679
00:45:55.458 --> 00:45:56.750
No way that's right.

680
00:45:57.417 --> 00:45:58.792
NORTHCOM confirms.

681
00:45:59.292 --> 00:46:01.292
Fort Greely's preparing to launch GBIs.

682
00:46:01.375 --> 00:46:04.333
{\an8}<i>That's right, Tony.
I've authorized weapons-release authority.</i>

683
00:46:13.083 --> 00:46:15.875
Um, sorry about that.
Seems we have an update.

684
00:46:17.542 --> 00:46:21.292
Current velocity indicates
the object will go suborbital.

685
00:46:22.583 --> 00:46:24.375
Current flight trajectory is consistent

686
00:46:24.458 --> 00:46:27.500
with impact somewhere
in the continental United States.

687
00:46:28.875 --> 00:46:30.083
Holy shit.

688
00:46:30.167 --> 00:46:32.125
<i>What's your level of confidence
on that, Tony?</i>

689
00:46:35.167 --> 00:46:36.333
<i>It's not an error.</i>

690
00:46:36.417 --> 00:46:39.042
We're tracking it
on multiple radar systems now.

691
00:46:40.250 --> 00:46:44.292
I'm told… Hi, Jerry.
…we have dual phenomenology on the track.

692
00:46:45.125 --> 00:46:46.958
Nineteen minutes to impact.

693
00:46:48.583 --> 00:46:50.542
<i>Confirming DEFCON 2.</i>

694
00:46:52.958 --> 00:46:55.083
<i>We have a confirmed
hostile launch, everyone.</i>

695
00:46:55.167 --> 00:46:56.667
Initiate phase one.

696
00:46:56.750 --> 00:46:59.375
OPLAN 8044, revision 25.

697
00:46:59.458 --> 00:47:01.583
- Stand by, all commands.
- Yes, sir.

698
00:47:01.667 --> 00:47:02.792
What is our target?

699
00:47:03.292 --> 00:47:05.333
My team's doing everything they can…

700
00:47:09.500 --> 00:47:11.167
Have you found POTUS yet?

701
00:47:12.958 --> 00:47:15.417
Okay, when you find him, patch him in.
Keep calling.

702
00:47:18.542 --> 00:47:20.542
Can I have 15 seconds?

703
00:47:35.375 --> 00:47:38.083
You gonna bring something back
every time we forward deploy?

704
00:47:38.667 --> 00:47:40.250
'Cause you're creating an expectation.

705
00:47:40.333 --> 00:47:42.875
He's three. He has no expectations.

706
00:47:42.958 --> 00:47:43.958
Exactly.

707
00:47:44.792 --> 00:47:47.750
Sometimes he wakes up, Daddy's gone.
Sometimes Daddy's home.

708
00:47:47.833 --> 00:47:51.333
Listen to him, kid.
It's the benefit of two marriages talking.

709
00:47:51.417 --> 00:47:52.833
Third time's the charm.

710
00:47:55.708 --> 00:47:57.625
<i>…with no warning whatsoever.</i>

711
00:47:57.708 --> 00:48:00.958
<i>- We need to speak with someone who can...
- Of course, Mr. Secretary.</i>

712
00:48:01.042 --> 00:48:02.958
Jake, how's Lily doing?

713
00:48:03.042 --> 00:48:05.417
- Sorry, I'm on a…
- Well, tell her I said hi.

714
00:48:05.500 --> 00:48:07.958
In the meantime,
we've raised our alert status.

715
00:48:08.583 --> 00:48:11.304
After last month's test launch,
we forward-deployed a number of B-2...

716
00:48:11.375 --> 00:48:12.625
<i>Hello? Uh…</i>

717
00:48:12.708 --> 00:48:17.458
<i>Sir, I'm sorry, I think, um…
I think we got disconnected for a minute.</i>

718
00:48:17.542 --> 00:48:19.333
<i>I think we should reconsider that, sir.</i>

719
00:48:19.417 --> 00:48:21.417
Reconsider what exactly?

720
00:48:21.500 --> 00:48:22.500
<i>Well…</i>

721
00:48:22.875 --> 00:48:25.333
By, uh… Go for it.

722
00:48:25.417 --> 00:48:27.500
By moving to DEFCON 2, sir,

723
00:48:27.583 --> 00:48:30.167
we are potentially risking
a spiral of alerts.

724
00:48:30.250 --> 00:48:31.542
<i>Spiral of what?</i>

725
00:48:32.167 --> 00:48:34.417
<i>Jake? Where the hell's Dick?</i>

726
00:48:34.500 --> 00:48:36.375
Spiral of alerts, Mr. Secretary.

727
00:48:36.458 --> 00:48:38.625
And, uh, Dick's out of pocket right now.

728
00:48:38.708 --> 00:48:41.583
<i>But… when we increase our readiness...</i>

729
00:48:41.667 --> 00:48:43.417
- Sir.
- Yeah.

730
00:48:43.500 --> 00:48:44.941
…all of our adversaries do the same,

731
00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:49.250
believing we're preparing to take
offensive action ourselves.

732
00:48:49.333 --> 00:48:52.042
Okay, what we need to do,
we need to communicate with them.

733
00:48:52.125 --> 00:48:55.333
- We need to… we need to explain our...
- <i>Then communicate.</i>

734
00:48:55.958 --> 00:48:57.375
<i>That's your job, not mine.</i>

735
00:48:58.250 --> 00:49:02.208
You have someone you can call who will
tell us just what the hell's going on?

736
00:49:02.292 --> 00:49:04.000
Don't let us hold you back.

737
00:49:04.083 --> 00:49:06.167
- Sir, put your phone in the tray.
- Just one sec.

738
00:49:06.250 --> 00:49:08.083
- I don't have one sec.
- <i>Yeah.</i>

739
00:49:08.167 --> 00:49:11.375
I'm sorry. Sorry, General.
I… I wasn't talking to you, sir.

740
00:49:11.458 --> 00:49:14.125
Then who in the hell were you talking to?

741
00:49:14.875 --> 00:49:17.000
<i>Do we have an ETA for POTUS yet?</i>

742
00:49:17.083 --> 00:49:18.583
<i>I'm told imminent.</i>

743
00:49:18.667 --> 00:49:22.875
<i>It occurs to me,
do we have COG responsibility here?</i>

744
00:49:23.583 --> 00:49:26.143
I'll be taking your questions
at the later briefing this morning,

745
00:49:26.167 --> 00:49:28.208
so if you can just hold them until then.

746
00:49:30.167 --> 00:49:31.250
Sorry.

747
00:49:31.333 --> 00:49:33.542
<i>Sorry. Excuse me.</i>

748
00:49:34.917 --> 00:49:36.542
We still waiting on POTUS?

749
00:49:38.458 --> 00:49:39.500
What do you think?

750
00:49:40.542 --> 00:49:41.833
I'd be guessing.

751
00:49:41.917 --> 00:49:43.333
Where the hell is POTUS?

752
00:49:43.417 --> 00:49:44.625
North Koreans.

753
00:49:45.917 --> 00:49:47.417
Fuel shortages. Crop failures.

754
00:49:47.500 --> 00:49:49.500
Maybe they're more desperate
than we thought.

755
00:49:50.667 --> 00:49:51.708
B-2s are sortieing.

756
00:49:51.792 --> 00:49:54.917
Or it's Moscow, and they want us to think
it's the North Koreans.

757
00:49:56.667 --> 00:49:58.667
Moscow knows we'll retaliate.

758
00:49:58.750 --> 00:49:59.750
Do they?

759
00:50:00.917 --> 00:50:02.792
Assassinating dissidents
wherever they please.

760
00:50:02.875 --> 00:50:05.250
Imprisoning Americans. Ukraine.

761
00:50:05.750 --> 00:50:08.875
And what? We confiscate
a few of their yachts in Saint-Tropez?

762
00:50:10.125 --> 00:50:12.500
A single, unattributed strike

763
00:50:13.000 --> 00:50:14.083
sows chaos,

764
00:50:14.583 --> 00:50:16.000
puts us on our heels,

765
00:50:16.500 --> 00:50:19.750
and it gives them an opportunity
to see if they can get away with worse.

766
00:50:19.833 --> 00:50:21.792
Gives everyone that opportunity.

767
00:50:23.750 --> 00:50:27.833
Or some fucking sub captain woke up,
found out his wife left him, and snapped.

768
00:50:27.917 --> 00:50:29.750
- Yeah.
- Told you I'm guessing.

769
00:50:30.250 --> 00:50:31.250
Sir.

770
00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:33.000
Battle gram.

771
00:50:34.333 --> 00:50:36.000
Updating our target package.

772
00:50:37.250 --> 00:50:39.625
We're still trying
to ascertain that for you, sir.

773
00:50:39.708 --> 00:50:42.208
Greely better not fuck this up.

774
00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:46.833
I have an updated impact estimate.

775
00:50:47.333 --> 00:50:48.375
{\an8}<i>Go ahead, Tony.</i>

776
00:51:08.750 --> 00:51:11.958
- Hey, when are we home again?
- 1700 next Tuesday.

777
00:51:12.042 --> 00:51:14.917
You think I can meet this girl
at the Applebee's before they close?

778
00:51:15.000 --> 00:51:18.500
- You take your dates to Applebee's?
- She works there, dumb-ass.

779
00:51:39.542 --> 00:51:41.542
<i>Jesus Christ.</i>

780
00:51:42.417 --> 00:51:46.125
{\an8}<i>This is why we have the GBIs.
No need to panic people.</i>

781
00:51:46.208 --> 00:51:47.833
<i>Did you say Chicago?</i>

782
00:51:47.917 --> 00:51:50.667
Uh, yes. In the medium bucket.

783
00:51:51.917 --> 00:51:53.875
<i>My daughter lives in Chicago.</i>

784
00:51:55.250 --> 00:51:59.708
<i>Sir, our GBIs
will be airborne momentarily.</i>

785
00:51:59.792 --> 00:52:01.083
<i>This is what we do.</i>

786
00:52:02.500 --> 00:52:03.667
{\an8}<i>Jake, you still there?</i>

787
00:52:03.750 --> 00:52:04.750
Yes, sir.

788
00:52:05.333 --> 00:52:08.500
<i>What are the chances this works?
Knocking it down.</i>

789
00:52:09.083 --> 00:52:11.333
- General Brady should answer.
<i>- I'm asking you.</i>

790
00:52:11.417 --> 00:52:13.875
<i>- Yes, but...
- I know what he's gonna say.</i>

791
00:52:13.958 --> 00:52:15.417
<i>And I want the truth.</i>

792
00:52:18.208 --> 00:52:20.583
I should stay in my lane, sir,

793
00:52:21.083 --> 00:52:23.917
but… …honestly…

794
00:52:24.000 --> 00:52:27.625
Interceptors have launched.
Everyone, interceptors have launched.

795
00:52:28.333 --> 00:52:31.125
<i>…It depends on the circumstances.</i>

796
00:52:31.875 --> 00:52:34.583
<i>Okay, when we… when we test…</i>

797
00:52:37.500 --> 00:52:39.125
When we test, we can't control...

798
00:52:39.208 --> 00:52:40.625
{\an8}<i>Cut the bullshit, damn it!</i>

799
00:52:43.833 --> 00:52:45.750
Once the kill vehicle separates,

800
00:52:45.833 --> 00:52:49.250
our mid course intercept system
has a success rate of 61%.

801
00:52:53.833 --> 00:52:55.417
<i>So it's a fucking coin toss?</i>

802
00:52:56.250 --> 00:52:58.792
<i>That's what $50 billion buys us?</i>

803
00:52:58.875 --> 00:53:01.292
We are talking about
hitting a bullet with a bullet.

804
00:53:01.792 --> 00:53:04.333
{\an8}<i>Hello? Hello? Can anyone hear me?</i>

805
00:53:04.417 --> 00:53:07.042
{\an8}<i>Mr. President, let's get you up to speed.</i>

806
00:53:07.917 --> 00:53:11.792
<i>Attention on the flight line.
Attention on the flight line.</i>

807
00:53:11.875 --> 00:53:13.875
<i>Ground crew to hangar three.</i>

808
00:53:13.958 --> 00:53:15.875
<i>Prep Ghost 1 for launch.</i>

809
00:53:17.958 --> 00:53:20.167
- This your office?
- Yeah.

810
00:53:20.250 --> 00:53:21.750
I need you to come with me, sir.

811
00:53:32.583 --> 00:53:34.750
<i>Fuel gauges checked!</i>

812
00:53:35.250 --> 00:53:37.833
<i>Flight controls.</i>

813
00:53:42.750 --> 00:53:43.958
<i>Munitions loaded.</i>

814
00:53:53.417 --> 00:53:55.708
Down the hall. Sir, we gotta move.

815
00:53:56.583 --> 00:53:59.333
- Sir, is everything okay?
- Gotta get to the elevator.

816
00:53:59.417 --> 00:54:02.208
- Marty, where are you going?
- Sir, we gotta get going now.

817
00:54:02.875 --> 00:54:03.875
Let's go.

818
00:54:41.958 --> 00:54:44.375
<i>- Could be a mistake.
- On our end or theirs?</i>

819
00:54:44.458 --> 00:54:45.458
<i>Who are they?</i>

820
00:54:45.542 --> 00:54:48.042
- Deputy NSA arriving.
- This way, sir.

821
00:54:49.208 --> 00:54:50.208
<i>Hold on.</i>

822
00:54:50.292 --> 00:54:54.792
<i>What I'm asking is, what are the odds
this is an intentional strike?</i>

823
00:54:54.875 --> 00:54:57.542
<i>The odds, I'd put them at 75%.</i>

824
00:54:58.125 --> 00:55:00.000
<i>I'd say 80%.</i>

825
00:55:00.083 --> 00:55:02.083
<i>All due respect, I'm closer to 50-50.</i>

826
00:55:02.167 --> 00:55:05.542
<i>Okay, is there anyone that can
do better than shot-in-the-dark guesses?</i>

827
00:55:05.625 --> 00:55:08.083
<i>We're not handicapping
the fucking Army-Navy game?</i>

828
00:55:08.167 --> 00:55:09.667
- Uh, Mr. President.
- <i>Yes.</i>

829
00:55:09.750 --> 00:55:12.875
<i>- Who's that?</i>
- This is, uh, Jake Baerington, sir.

830
00:55:12.958 --> 00:55:17.500
Um, we actually met briefly
before the, uh, G8 last year.

831
00:55:18.375 --> 00:55:19.375
Uh…

832
00:55:21.750 --> 00:55:24.167
If someone could…
If… if we could get Anna Park.

833
00:55:24.250 --> 00:55:26.917
She's the national intelligence officer
for the DPRK.

834
00:55:27.000 --> 00:55:29.000
She'll have a more informed view

835
00:55:29.083 --> 00:55:31.003
on North Korean
intentions and capabilities, sir.

836
00:55:31.042 --> 00:55:33.167
<i>Okay, so how do I talk to her?</i>

837
00:55:33.250 --> 00:55:35.167
We're getting her for you,
uh, Mr. President.

838
00:55:35.250 --> 00:55:37.458
Company men, ready!

839
00:55:38.375 --> 00:55:39.500
Fire!

840
00:55:43.292 --> 00:55:44.708
Wow!

841
00:55:49.667 --> 00:55:51.292
I'm gonna have to call the office.

842
00:55:53.875 --> 00:55:55.875
- Hello?
- Hey, Anna. It's Jake.

843
00:55:55.958 --> 00:55:59.333
- <i>Jake. I just got a JEEP alert.</i>
- You're on an NSCC with the president.

844
00:55:59.417 --> 00:56:01.958
- I'm sorry, what?
- <i>Hey, Miss Park.</i>

845
00:56:02.042 --> 00:56:03.417
<i>It's the president.</i>

846
00:56:03.500 --> 00:56:06.250
<i>I understand that you're…
you're the expert.</i>

847
00:56:06.333 --> 00:56:10.250
{\an8}There was a launch, Anna,
about ten minutes ago. Not a test.

848
00:56:10.750 --> 00:56:11.917
{\an8}Okay, we need answers.

849
00:56:12.417 --> 00:56:16.375
{\an8}Starting with could the DPRK have
an SSBN capability we don't know about?

850
00:56:16.458 --> 00:56:19.583
And how likely is it that the regime
would initiate a strike like this?

851
00:56:20.875 --> 00:56:22.958
A launch? I mean…

852
00:56:23.792 --> 00:56:25.625
Jake, I'm sorry. I'm off today.

853
00:56:25.708 --> 00:56:28.042
<i>- Okay? I'm not even…</i>
- Anna, what the… Where are you?

854
00:56:28.125 --> 00:56:29.667
- What the hell?
- <i>Gettysburg.</i>

855
00:56:29.750 --> 00:56:30.875
Anna.

856
00:56:32.125 --> 00:56:34.208
Please, this is real.

857
00:56:35.208 --> 00:56:38.542
I can't answer either question
with certainty, but yes,

858
00:56:38.625 --> 00:56:42.167
they've absolutely been seeking
a sea-based launch capability.

859
00:56:42.250 --> 00:56:45.250
They deployed a modified Romeo-class sub
two years ago

860
00:56:45.333 --> 00:56:48.167
carrying ten short-range cruise missiles.

861
00:56:48.250 --> 00:56:51.042
<i>But why? Why… why would they do this?</i>

862
00:56:51.125 --> 00:56:53.750
<i>The regime's primary motivation
is self-preservation.</i>

863
00:56:53.833 --> 00:56:55.292
<i>Wouldn't that discourage?</i>

864
00:56:55.375 --> 00:56:58.500
Sir, they may believe
they can survive a retaliatory strike.

865
00:56:58.583 --> 00:57:01.583
Which, given their dispersed command
and control and mobile-launch system,

866
00:57:01.667 --> 00:57:03.333
yes, it's entirely possible.

867
00:57:03.417 --> 00:57:07.375
And then negotiate relief for themselves.
Um, no more launches in exchange for aid.

868
00:57:07.458 --> 00:57:09.375
<i>They think they can blackmail us?</i>

869
00:57:09.458 --> 00:57:12.083
If you're losing a board game,
you might as well topple it.

870
00:57:12.167 --> 00:57:14.708
<i>Miss Park,
this is General Brady at STRATCOM.</i>

871
00:57:14.792 --> 00:57:16.708
Last time I checked,

872
00:57:17.208 --> 00:57:20.250
Moscow's not exactly
winning the game either.

873
00:57:20.333 --> 00:57:24.125
<i>You're not wrong, sir.
The Russians are stretched and cornered.</i>

874
00:57:24.208 --> 00:57:26.833
<i>They've been coordinating
more closely with Beijing.</i>

875
00:57:26.917 --> 00:57:29.792
They've grown far more aggressive
with their sub deployment.

876
00:57:30.292 --> 00:57:33.083
Where exactly in the Pacific
did the launch originate?

877
00:57:33.167 --> 00:57:35.250
We can't be precise, ma'am.

878
00:57:35.333 --> 00:57:37.458
DSP satellites missed it.

879
00:57:37.542 --> 00:57:38.958
You're fucking kidding?

880
00:57:39.042 --> 00:57:42.125
<i>Why the hell does that matter?
We're tracking them now, aren't we?</i>

881
00:57:42.208 --> 00:57:44.250
{\an8}Yes, uh, Mr. President, we are.

882
00:57:44.333 --> 00:57:47.167
It's just that blinding a DSP satellite,

883
00:57:47.250 --> 00:57:49.708
it could indicate
that we've been compromised.

884
00:57:49.792 --> 00:57:52.042
<i>A cyber penetration
of our command-and-control systems.</i>

885
00:57:52.125 --> 00:57:53.583
Seven, eight…

886
00:57:53.667 --> 00:57:57.375
Which would strongly suggest
a sophisticated, coordinated assault

887
00:57:57.458 --> 00:57:59.000
that is only just beginning.

888
00:57:59.083 --> 00:58:01.000
<i>There's no hard evidence of that.</i>

889
00:58:01.083 --> 00:58:02.375
<i>We'd need more information.</i>

890
00:58:02.458 --> 00:58:06.083
The Chinese navy has been experimenting
with AI-assisted launch systems,

891
00:58:06.167 --> 00:58:09.042
so this could be a technical mishap.

892
00:58:09.125 --> 00:58:12.167
<i>All right, that's enough
of this. This is a waste of time.</i>

893
00:58:12.250 --> 00:58:14.792
Sir, a… a cyber expert could potentially...

894
00:58:14.875 --> 00:58:17.875
<i>Yeah, well, find one, okay?</i>

895
00:58:17.958 --> 00:58:20.417
EKV has separated from the first GBI.

896
00:58:21.417 --> 00:58:22.625
One minute to intercept.

897
00:58:22.708 --> 00:58:24.292
- Aiden!
- Boo!

898
00:58:25.417 --> 00:58:27.000
<i>Ma'am, I'm disconnecting you now.</i>

899
00:58:27.083 --> 00:58:29.708
- <i>Okay.</i>
- If you have a JEEP alert, get moving.

900
00:58:29.792 --> 00:58:31.375
Mom? What happened?

901
00:58:35.708 --> 00:58:37.333
Left! Right!

902
00:58:37.417 --> 00:58:38.917
Right! Right!

903
00:58:39.000 --> 00:58:41.208
Left! Right!

904
00:58:45.375 --> 00:58:47.583
At ease!

905
00:58:48.583 --> 00:58:49.917
<i>Ten seconds.</i>

906
00:58:50.792 --> 00:58:51.792
<i>Nine.</i>

907
00:58:52.375 --> 00:58:53.542
<i>Eight.</i>

908
00:58:53.625 --> 00:58:55.333
<i>- Seven.
- Before, with the chips...</i>

909
00:58:55.417 --> 00:58:57.542
<i>- We're good, man. I'm a slob.
- Six. Five…</i>

910
00:58:57.625 --> 00:58:59.917
<i>To hell with her.
Shouldn't have left it like that.</i>

911
00:59:00.417 --> 00:59:01.500
<i>Three.</i>

912
00:59:02.000 --> 00:59:03.458
<i>- Two.
- Yeah.</i>

913
00:59:04.083 --> 00:59:05.083
<i>One.</i>

914
00:59:13.875 --> 00:59:15.042
<i>Confirm impact.</i>

915
00:59:18.167 --> 00:59:20.500
<i>- Confirm impact.
- Stand by. Confirming.</i>

916
00:59:24.583 --> 00:59:26.375
<i>What are you waiting for?</i>

917
00:59:29.667 --> 00:59:31.333
- <i>It's negative.</i>
- What'd he say?

918
00:59:32.333 --> 00:59:33.625
What did he say?

919
00:59:34.667 --> 00:59:35.667
<i>I, um…</i>

920
00:59:36.875 --> 00:59:38.250
{\an8}<i>Negative impact.</i>

921
00:59:39.375 --> 00:59:40.875
<i>Object remains inbound.</i>

922
00:59:46.125 --> 00:59:49.292
Like Baker said… coin toss.

923
00:59:51.583 --> 00:59:54.167
{\an8}<i>We did every fucking thing right.</i>

924
00:59:54.250 --> 00:59:57.167
{\an8}Mr. President, confirming DEFCON 1, sir.

925
00:59:58.250 --> 01:00:01.250
<i>Oh Jesus. We just went DEFCON 1.</i>

926
01:00:01.333 --> 01:00:02.417
<i>Confirming.</i>

927
01:00:15.917 --> 01:00:17.042
What now, sir?

928
01:00:18.250 --> 01:00:19.750
There is no plan B.

929
01:00:20.417 --> 01:00:22.250
Yes, it's a negative.

930
01:00:22.333 --> 01:00:25.583
- What do we do now?
- I don't know. I don't know.

931
01:00:25.667 --> 01:00:26.833
Yes, confirming.

932
01:00:43.625 --> 01:00:45.375
Sir, Black Book's available.

933
01:00:48.500 --> 01:00:50.292
<i>Why the hell is that book out, son?</i>

934
01:00:50.375 --> 01:00:53.750
Mr. President, significant time
and expertise were devoted

935
01:00:53.833 --> 01:00:55.542
to designing these options.

936
01:00:55.625 --> 01:00:59.375
You'll find a range,
select, limited, and major,

937
01:00:59.458 --> 01:01:02.292
depending on the scale of the response
you feel is warranted.

938
01:01:02.375 --> 01:01:05.500
I suggest you allow
Lieutenant Commander Reeves to brief you.

939
01:01:06.000 --> 01:01:08.292
Three 055 Renhai-class destroyers
on the move.

940
01:01:08.375 --> 01:01:13.042
Jesus Christ. I got action in Khorramabad.
Sirens in Tel Aviv, sir.

941
01:01:13.125 --> 01:01:14.958
Everybody knows we missed.

942
01:01:16.667 --> 01:01:19.583
Mr. President, we're seeing
some concerning activity

943
01:01:19.667 --> 01:01:21.667
from our adversaries
on a number of fronts.

944
01:01:21.750 --> 01:01:24.083
<i>More concerning
than a goddamn nuclear launch?</i>

945
01:01:24.167 --> 01:01:29.000
Sir, the USS Virginia reports
it's just lost contact with its shadow,

946
01:01:29.083 --> 01:01:32.708
one of four Russian submarines
we're tracking in the North Atlantic,

947
01:01:32.792 --> 01:01:36.333
each presumably armed with 16 SLBMs.

948
01:01:36.417 --> 01:01:39.375
Until we know differently,
we have to assume this may get worse.

949
01:01:39.458 --> 01:01:43.000
{\an8}<i>General Brady, I know
everyone's trying to do their jobs here,</i>

950
01:01:43.542 --> 01:01:45.250
{\an8}<i>but we need to slow the fuck down.</i>

951
01:01:46.375 --> 01:01:47.625
<i>President's right.</i>

952
01:01:47.708 --> 01:01:49.833
There's no way
he can make an informed decision

953
01:01:49.917 --> 01:01:51.333
under these circumstances.

954
01:01:51.417 --> 01:01:53.792
<i>Mr. President, Mr. Baerington,</i>

955
01:01:53.875 --> 01:01:57.000
<i>slowing down is one luxury
we just don't have.</i>

956
01:01:57.708 --> 01:01:59.625
These are the circumstances.

957
01:01:59.708 --> 01:02:03.833
In little more than seven minutes,
we will lose the city of Chicago.

958
01:02:03.917 --> 01:02:05.750
I can't tell you why.

959
01:02:06.458 --> 01:02:09.833
Or why we're seeing
North Korea, Russia, China,

960
01:02:09.917 --> 01:02:13.458
Pakistan, and even Iran
raising their alerts

961
01:02:13.542 --> 01:02:16.875
and mobilizing their forces
across air, land, and sea.

962
01:02:18.083 --> 01:02:20.917
Perhaps, as Mr. Baerington
suggested earlier,

963
01:02:21.000 --> 01:02:24.833
<i>they are simply and innocently
responding to our posture.</i>

964
01:02:24.917 --> 01:02:26.417
<i>It is also possible</i>

965
01:02:26.500 --> 01:02:30.833
<i>that they've seen our homeland
is about to absorb a catastrophic blow,</i>

966
01:02:30.917 --> 01:02:33.500
<i>and they are readying
to take advantage of that.</i>

967
01:02:33.583 --> 01:02:37.333
Or this is all part of
a phased, coordinated assault,

968
01:02:37.417 --> 01:02:38.833
with far worse to come.

969
01:02:38.917 --> 01:02:40.417
I simply don't know.

970
01:02:40.500 --> 01:02:42.792
What I do know is this.

971
01:02:42.875 --> 01:02:48.375
If we do not take steps
to neutralize our enemies now,

972
01:02:48.458 --> 01:02:51.125
we will lose our window to do so.

973
01:02:51.208 --> 01:02:53.375
<i>We can strike preemptively,</i>

974
01:02:53.458 --> 01:02:57.333
<i>or risk 100 ICBMs launching our way,</i>

975
01:02:57.417 --> 01:03:01.083
at which time,
this war will have already been lost.

976
01:03:05.875 --> 01:03:07.375
{\an8}<i>And if there is no war?</i>

977
01:03:10.000 --> 01:03:10.833
<i>If this is it?</i>

978
01:03:10.917 --> 01:03:13.958
I think we'd all welcome
any indication of that.

979
01:03:14.042 --> 01:03:17.375
{\an8}As unfathomable as it was
just five minutes ago,

980
01:03:17.458 --> 01:03:19.667
{\an8}I'd accept the loss
of ten million Americans

981
01:03:19.750 --> 01:03:22.833
{\an8}if I could be absolutely certain
it stops there.

982
01:03:22.917 --> 01:03:27.250
Of course, in absence of that certainty,
we can all certainly say a prayer

983
01:03:27.333 --> 01:03:31.750
{\an8}and rely on the goodwill
of our adversaries to keep us safe.

984
01:03:31.833 --> 01:03:36.417
{\an8}Or we can hit their command centers,
silos, and bombers

985
01:03:36.500 --> 01:03:38.292
while they're still on the ground,

986
01:03:38.375 --> 01:03:42.333
eliminating their ability
to take further action against us.

987
01:03:44.667 --> 01:03:47.833
We've already lost
one American city today.

988
01:03:49.333 --> 01:03:50.625
How many more do you wanna risk?

989
01:03:50.708 --> 01:03:52.333
<i>What kind of question is that?</i>

990
01:03:53.625 --> 01:03:56.417
<i>- This is insanity, okay?</i>
- No, sir.

991
01:03:58.458 --> 01:03:59.958
This is reality.

992
01:04:00.542 --> 01:04:01.833
Six minutes to impact.

993
01:04:01.917 --> 01:04:05.208
It's Walker. She's got
the Russian foreign minister on the line.

994
01:04:05.292 --> 01:04:06.792
We can't merge the calls.

995
01:04:09.250 --> 01:04:10.250
Jake.

996
01:04:10.917 --> 01:04:13.018
Sit room has
the Russian foreign minister on the line,

997
01:04:13.042 --> 01:04:15.000
but we cannot merge the call.

998
01:04:15.750 --> 01:04:18.500
You need to pick up and take it.

999
01:04:19.792 --> 01:04:21.625
It has to be you.

1000
01:04:23.208 --> 01:04:24.208
Okay?

1001
01:04:24.833 --> 01:04:28.333
The president needs a reason
not to retaliate, okay? You give him one.

1002
01:04:31.083 --> 01:04:32.417
- You ready?
- Yeah.

1003
01:04:33.083 --> 01:04:34.250
Let's go.

1004
01:04:35.542 --> 01:04:37.458
This is Jake Baerington.

1005
01:04:37.542 --> 01:04:41.208
- I'm the deputy national security advisor.
- <i>You authorized to speak?</i>

1006
01:04:41.292 --> 01:04:44.583
I'm authorized to do whatever's necessary
to de-escalate this situation, sir.

1007
01:04:44.667 --> 01:04:48.875
<i>Your bombers are airborne.
What kind of de-escalation is that?</i>

1008
01:04:48.958 --> 01:04:50.292
Mr. Foreign Minister,

1009
01:04:50.375 --> 01:04:52.708
you have to understand
that's only a precaution.

1010
01:04:53.583 --> 01:04:55.458
Okay, our country is about to be hit

1011
01:04:55.542 --> 01:04:58.708
by an entirely unprecedented
and unprovoked attack.

1012
01:04:58.792 --> 01:05:00.875
<i>Which we had nothing to do with.</i>

1013
01:05:00.958 --> 01:05:02.333
Do I have your word?

1014
01:05:02.417 --> 01:05:05.333
Can I assure the president
that Russia has nothing to do with this,

1015
01:05:05.417 --> 01:05:08.625
<i>they're not behind the launch,
and you will not seek to capitalize?</i>

1016
01:05:08.708 --> 01:05:09.708
Yes.

1017
01:05:10.542 --> 01:05:11.875
And do I have your word

1018
01:05:12.542 --> 01:05:15.875
that you won't use it as an excuse
to wipe us out?

1019
01:05:15.958 --> 01:05:18.167
- That's ridiculous.
- <i>Is it?</i>

1020
01:05:18.250 --> 01:05:19.708
<i>You might tell your president,</i>

1021
01:05:19.792 --> 01:05:24.458
<i>if your forces do not stand down,
we will be compelled to respond in kind.</i>

1022
01:05:25.250 --> 01:05:28.083
You have a sub off our coast
that just slipped its shadow.

1023
01:05:28.167 --> 01:05:31.208
<i>Order it to the surface
to identify its location</i>

1024
01:05:31.292 --> 01:05:32.625
<i>as a show of good faith.</i>

1025
01:05:32.708 --> 01:05:34.792
So you can wipe it out of the water?

1026
01:05:34.875 --> 01:05:37.333
We are running out of time,

1027
01:05:37.417 --> 01:05:39.083
and my wife is six months…

1028
01:05:41.667 --> 01:05:42.667
<i>Jake.</i>

1029
01:05:42.750 --> 01:05:44.458
I'm sorry. Um…

1030
01:05:46.500 --> 01:05:47.750
Jake?

1031
01:05:47.833 --> 01:05:49.625
<i>Listen, if we get this wrong,</i>

1032
01:05:50.458 --> 01:05:52.458
none of us are gonna be alive tomorrow.

1033
01:05:52.542 --> 01:05:55.125
Now, if you're telling me
that you didn't do this,

1034
01:05:55.208 --> 01:05:56.542
<i>and I believe you,</i>

1035
01:05:56.625 --> 01:05:59.542
<i>then I can promise you
we will not hit any Russian targets.</i>

1036
01:05:59.625 --> 01:06:03.958
<i>Can you promise me you will stand down
your long-range strategic assets?</i>

1037
01:06:04.042 --> 01:06:06.958
<i>Better. There'll be no retaliation at all.</i>

1038
01:06:07.042 --> 01:06:08.125
I completely agree.

1039
01:06:08.208 --> 01:06:11.208
<i>And I will push for that,
but that is not my decision, sir.</i>

1040
01:06:11.292 --> 01:06:13.208
If you do retaliate,

1041
01:06:13.292 --> 01:06:18.000
can you guarantee that your response
will not infringe on our airspace?

1042
01:06:22.583 --> 01:06:25.000
With our bombers, yes, of course.

1043
01:06:25.083 --> 01:06:26.333
And missiles?

1044
01:06:26.417 --> 01:06:29.917
If you determine that, God,
fucking China is responsible...

1045
01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:32.083
- Sir, there…
- Tell the truth.

1046
01:06:32.792 --> 01:06:33.792
No.

1047
01:06:37.125 --> 01:06:39.667
Sir, we both know
that there would be some overflight.

1048
01:06:39.750 --> 01:06:41.167
<i>There's no way around that.</i>

1049
01:06:41.250 --> 01:06:43.917
And you expect us to simply trust

1050
01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:47.250
that warheads flying over our head
are not destined on our cities?

1051
01:06:47.333 --> 01:06:50.042
<i>Hopefully, sir,
there will not be any warheads.</i>

1052
01:06:51.000 --> 01:06:55.542
If there are, then, yes,
I'm asking you to trust me.

1053
01:06:59.458 --> 01:07:00.667
Trust.

1054
01:07:01.708 --> 01:07:02.708
Why?

1055
01:07:04.083 --> 01:07:06.250
<i>- I'll talk to my president.</i>
- What if, um...

1056
01:07:14.208 --> 01:07:15.875
<i>Darkstar, this is Ghost 1.</i>

1057
01:07:15.958 --> 01:07:17.625
Approaching loiter position.

1058
01:07:19.500 --> 01:07:21.750
<i>Ghost 1-1, Darkstar. Picture clean.</i>

1059
01:07:21.833 --> 01:07:23.458
<i>Stand by mission data package.</i>

1060
01:07:31.083 --> 01:07:32.667
Is this right?

1061
01:07:33.625 --> 01:07:35.833
Darkstar, Ghost. MDB confirmed.

1062
01:07:37.792 --> 01:07:40.333
<i>Ghost, Darkstar. Stand by execution order.</i>

1063
01:07:42.708 --> 01:07:45.250
Forward-deployed B-2s
are at loitering position.

1064
01:07:45.333 --> 01:07:47.833
Mr. President,
we're going to need your decision.

1065
01:07:48.333 --> 01:07:51.750
Lieutenant Commander Reeves
is your strike advisor

1066
01:07:52.250 --> 01:07:55.500
and can walk you through
the authentication process.

1067
01:07:55.583 --> 01:07:59.000
Then you'll need to read aloud
an attack option designation...

1068
01:07:59.083 --> 01:08:01.500
<i>Yeah. Look,
I understand all that, all right?</i>

1069
01:08:01.583 --> 01:08:03.708
<i>Reid, I need you.</i>

1070
01:08:05.583 --> 01:08:06.833
<i>What do you think, Reid?</i>

1071
01:08:06.917 --> 01:08:08.708
<i>We're close to take off.</i>

1072
01:08:08.792 --> 01:08:10.000
<i>Did we lose him?</i>

1073
01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:12.542
{\an8}<i>Sir! No, no, no, no, sir!</i>

1074
01:08:13.042 --> 01:08:14.833
{\an8}<i>Holy shit!</i>

1075
01:08:15.417 --> 01:08:16.917
- <i>What was that?</i>
- All right.

1076
01:08:17.000 --> 01:08:18.542
<i>Mr. President?</i>

1077
01:08:18.625 --> 01:08:21.375
<i>- It's Jake again, sir. Baerington.</i>
- Keep your seats. Keep your seats.

1078
01:08:21.458 --> 01:08:23.500
{\an8}<i>I spoke to the Russian foreign minister.</i>

1079
01:08:23.583 --> 01:08:26.958
He denies their responsibility
for the launch.

1080
01:08:27.625 --> 01:08:30.750
Said he spoke to Beijing,
and he doesn't think it was them either.

1081
01:08:33.417 --> 01:08:35.917
- I believed him, sir.
- <i>You did?</i>

1082
01:08:36.500 --> 01:08:39.667
<i>- They gonna back down?</i>
- Sir, I think that they want to.

1083
01:08:40.750 --> 01:08:43.417
And if we can guarantee
that we will not retaliate,

1084
01:08:43.500 --> 01:08:44.875
I think I can, uh…

1085
01:08:46.417 --> 01:08:48.417
We can convince them.

1086
01:08:48.500 --> 01:08:51.042
<i>- What does that mean?
- We don't launch.</i>

1087
01:08:51.958 --> 01:08:53.250
<i>Against anyone.</i>

1088
01:08:53.917 --> 01:08:55.000
<i>For now, at least.</i>

1089
01:08:55.083 --> 01:08:57.833
<i>What, we just sit back
and watch Chicago incinerate?</i>

1090
01:08:58.375 --> 01:09:01.667
{\an8}<i>Are you fucking kidding me? Do you think
the American people are gonna go for that?</i>

1091
01:09:01.750 --> 01:09:04.625
<i>Sir, the… the warhead,
it might still malfunction.</i>

1092
01:09:04.708 --> 01:09:06.333
<i>They do that sometimes.</i>

1093
01:09:06.417 --> 01:09:08.667
<i>Did he agree to these terms?</i>

1094
01:09:09.167 --> 01:09:12.292
<i>All right, we do nothing,
they back off for certain?</i>

1095
01:09:12.375 --> 01:09:14.375
- More or less.
- <i>More or less?!</i>

1096
01:09:14.458 --> 01:09:15.875
<i>- Jake.
- Yes, sir.</i>

1097
01:09:15.958 --> 01:09:17.833
<i>I'm gonna need you to breathe.</i>

1098
01:09:17.917 --> 01:09:19.077
I'm breathing just fine, sir.

1099
01:09:19.125 --> 01:09:22.667
<i>Good 'cause my job is
to make this decision. I wish it weren't.</i>

1100
01:09:22.750 --> 01:09:26.375
<i>And your job is to tell me
exactly what he agreed to.</i>

1101
01:09:27.250 --> 01:09:30.167
<i>- No bullshit. Can you do that?</i>
- He didn't agree to anything, sir.

1102
01:09:30.250 --> 01:09:32.083
He said
he needed to speak with his president.

1103
01:09:32.583 --> 01:09:35.042
Sounds to me like we know nothing new.

1104
01:09:35.125 --> 01:09:37.833
<i>Wrong, General. If we do what he's asking,</i>

1105
01:09:37.917 --> 01:09:40.000
<i>if we hold back,
there's at least a chance.</i>

1106
01:09:40.083 --> 01:09:41.542
Two minutes and 30 seconds.

1107
01:09:41.625 --> 01:09:44.583
<i>Jake, Jake, I do what you're suggesting,</i>

1108
01:09:45.792 --> 01:09:48.042
<i>I let whoever did this get away with it.</i>

1109
01:09:48.542 --> 01:09:50.500
<i>How is that any different
from surrendering?</i>

1110
01:09:50.583 --> 01:09:52.542
<i>Sir, if you wanna look at it that way,</i>

1111
01:09:53.167 --> 01:09:55.500
then I'm telling you your choices are

1112
01:09:55.583 --> 01:09:57.083
surrender or suicide.

1113
01:10:01.875 --> 01:10:03.000
Uh…

1114
01:10:08.333 --> 01:10:09.667
<i>We gonna need a minute.</i>

1115
01:10:11.833 --> 01:10:13.333
So what now? What are we doing?

1116
01:10:14.417 --> 01:10:16.042
Now I call Fort Belvoir.

1117
01:10:16.125 --> 01:10:18.667
Put the Army Corps of Engineers
on standby.

1118
01:10:19.667 --> 01:10:22.583
In case the White House gets hit
and they need to dig us out.

1119
01:10:22.667 --> 01:10:23.667
Oh God.

1120
01:10:23.708 --> 01:10:25.667
- Serious?
- That's the plan.

1121
01:10:27.583 --> 01:10:29.000
There's a plan for this?

1122
01:10:38.917 --> 01:10:40.375
If this order comes through…

1123
01:10:42.875 --> 01:10:44.375
I know my job, sir.

1124
01:11:00.167 --> 01:11:05.292
<i>Romeo, Bravo, Juliett, Whiskey,
Delta, Foxtrot, Echo.</i>

1125
01:11:05.375 --> 01:11:07.333
Missilization order is authentic.

1126
01:11:08.917 --> 01:11:10.500
Romeo, Bravo, Juliett,

1127
01:11:10.583 --> 01:11:13.125
Whiskey, Delta, Foxtrot, Echo.

1128
01:11:13.208 --> 01:11:14.583
I concur with missilization.

1129
01:11:15.667 --> 01:11:16.792
Three, two, one. Turn.

1130
01:11:16.875 --> 01:11:18.750
Sir, standing by for fire order.

1131
01:11:20.042 --> 01:11:22.083
Sir, your nuclear forces are ready.

1132
01:11:22.583 --> 01:11:24.792
- Sir, B-2s are at loiter.
- Yes, sir.

1133
01:11:24.875 --> 01:11:27.083
{\an8}Missile field status green.

1134
01:11:27.167 --> 01:11:28.917
{\an8}What if he doesn't come back on?

1135
01:11:30.542 --> 01:11:34.042
Decapitation event.
We find the vice president.

1136
01:11:34.125 --> 01:11:37.958
If we can't reach him, speaker.
Right on down the list.

1137
01:11:38.042 --> 01:11:39.167
<i>I'm here.</i>

1138
01:11:40.083 --> 01:11:42.917
<i>- You'll need your SAS card, sir.
- Oh.</i>

1139
01:11:45.708 --> 01:11:47.208
<i>It's in here somewhere.</i>

1140
01:11:48.042 --> 01:11:49.125
<i>Right.</i>

1141
01:11:50.042 --> 01:11:51.917
<i>Reminds me of when I was in college.</i>

1142
01:11:54.958 --> 01:11:57.208
<i>You just, uh, read it aloud.</i>

1143
01:11:59.708 --> 01:12:02.500
{\an8}<i>November, Delta, Oscar.</i>

1144
01:12:03.000 --> 01:12:06.000
{\an8}<i>One, one, one, seven.</i>

1145
01:12:06.083 --> 01:12:08.500
November, Delta, Oscar.

1146
01:12:08.583 --> 01:12:11.542
<i>One, one, one, seven.</i>

1147
01:12:13.333 --> 01:12:15.833
<i>National command authority confirmed.</i>

1148
01:12:17.625 --> 01:12:19.458
Your orders, Mr. President?

1149
01:12:20.208 --> 01:12:21.375
<i>My orders?</i>

1150
01:13:01.417 --> 01:13:03.708
You sure you don't want any coffee? Water?

1151
01:13:04.208 --> 01:13:05.625
No, thank you, ma'am.

1152
01:13:21.875 --> 01:13:24.167
Betty, can you get us the majority leader?

1153
01:13:24.250 --> 01:13:26.750
Quickly, please. Thanks.

1154
01:13:28.708 --> 01:13:30.500
Already 45 minutes late.

1155
01:13:33.583 --> 01:13:35.417
POTUS for majority leader, please.

1156
01:13:36.500 --> 01:13:37.500
Thank you.

1157
01:14:02.917 --> 01:14:04.625
That's looking more like it.

1158
01:14:22.125 --> 01:14:23.208
Nope.

1159
01:14:23.792 --> 01:14:25.125
Out playing nine.

1160
01:14:26.583 --> 01:14:28.042
It's going, I guess.

1161
01:14:28.542 --> 01:14:31.958
Last time I was around all these uniforms,
I was a private.

1162
01:14:32.583 --> 01:14:34.500
They're still full of shit.

1163
01:14:40.458 --> 01:14:42.500
Thanks, George. I appreciate that.

1164
01:14:43.625 --> 01:14:46.375
We were lucky to have 33 great years.

1165
01:14:47.083 --> 01:14:49.875
Meant the world you and Sheila
came to the funeral.

1166
01:14:52.083 --> 01:14:54.458
Okay, talk later.

1167
01:14:58.875 --> 01:14:59.875
Sir.

1168
01:15:01.000 --> 01:15:02.000
Sir.

1169
01:15:02.833 --> 01:15:04.208
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

1170
01:15:07.083 --> 01:15:08.583
Let's knock this in now.

1171
01:15:14.625 --> 01:15:16.833
<i>Hey. I was hoping to catch you.</i>

1172
01:15:17.542 --> 01:15:20.625
- I wish you were here to see this.
- <i>Yeah? Is it going good?</i>

1173
01:15:20.708 --> 01:15:23.708
<i>They say anything
that raises awareness helps.</i>

1174
01:15:23.792 --> 01:15:26.292
- Okay.
- <i>You sound tired.</i>

1175
01:15:26.792 --> 01:15:28.583
No. Um…

1176
01:15:29.208 --> 01:15:30.208
I'm fine.

1177
01:15:31.250 --> 01:15:35.083
My husband, the only politician
who can't lie to save his life.

1178
01:15:35.167 --> 01:15:36.958
Okay. I'm fucked.

1179
01:15:37.042 --> 01:15:39.208
You know, didn't they, uh,

1180
01:15:40.167 --> 01:15:41.792
promise that, uh,

1181
01:15:42.292 --> 01:15:44.125
we'd get used to it after a while?

1182
01:15:44.208 --> 01:15:47.083
<i>"Worse than the campaign."
I think that's what I remember.</i>

1183
01:15:47.167 --> 01:15:49.667
<i>I think they said
it would break us, actually.</i>

1184
01:15:49.750 --> 01:15:52.750
Oh, speaking of,
we have to talk about my mother.

1185
01:15:53.667 --> 01:15:56.333
Now the doctor's saying
she needs full-time help.

1186
01:15:59.292 --> 01:16:01.458
Hello? Are you there?

1187
01:16:01.958 --> 01:16:03.958
It's not just me. It's the doctor.

1188
01:16:04.042 --> 01:16:07.875
